> 
> - **`model_id`**: the semantic model identity you choose between.  
>   Examples: `gpt-4o`, `gpt-5.4-mini`, `claude-sonnet-4`, `gemini-2.5-flash`.
> 
> - **`model_version`**: a specific revision of that same named model, usually needed for reproducibility and silent provider updates.  
>   Examples: `2026-09-01`, `snapshot-abc123`, `openai-api-2026-09`, or your own registration revision such as `"2"`.
> 
> So registrations might look like:
> 
> ```python
> Planner.register_model(
>     OpenAIAdapter.from_env("gpt-5.4-mini"),
>     model_id="gpt-5.4-mini",
>     version="2026-09-01",
>     quality_prior=0.85,
> )
> ```
> 
> If OpenAI later changes behavior under the same provider name:
> 
> ```python
> Planner.register_model(
>     OpenAIAdapter.from_env("gpt-5.4-mini"),
>     model_id="gpt-5.4-mini",
>     version="2026-11-15",
>     quality_prior=0.85,
> )
> ```
> 
