> ```
> 
> Register it with JavaScript exposure:
> 
> ```python
> tool = make_llm_smart_tool(router, registry, repository, runtime)
> 
> Planner.register_tool(
>     name=tool.name,
>     description=tool.description,
>     fn=tool.fn,
>     config=tool.config,
>     version=tool.version,
>     metadata={
>         "javascript": {
>             "name": "llm.smart",
>             "arguments": {
>                 "prompt": "string",
>                 "min_quality": "number?",
>                 "max_tokens": "number?",
>             },
>         }
>     },
> )
> ```
> 
> Also fix `JavaScriptRuntime.execute`: initialize `process = None` immediately before its `try:` block, since its `finally` currently can reference it before assignment.
